      "textEn": "327\n\nMeaning of the word\n\nSa—that; Api—also; Tam—to him; Chakme—started wanting; Vikshya—looking; Narinam—of women; Hridayam—heart; Gamam—to the heart; Churanewali—stealing; Hasanti—laughing; Vridita—full of shyness; Apangi—casting a slanted gaze; Tat—on him; Nyasta—stable;\nHridaya—heart; Ikshana—and eyes. Arjun was extremely attractive to women, therefore, as soon as Subhadra saw him, she desired to get him as her husband. With a charming smile and wry glances, she fixed her heart\nand her eyes on them. Meaning: As soon as Subhadra saw, she realized that Arjun was not a sanyasi (ascetic), but her beloved.\nIs. In Lord Krishna, Srila Prabhupada describes this in detail, \"Maharaj, Parikshit's grandfather\nArjun himself was exceptionally handsome, and his physical structure was extremely attractive to Subhadra. Subhadra also decided in her mind that she would accept only Arjun as her husband.\nShe will accept only Arjun as her husband.\nLike a normal girl, she was smiling with great joy seeing Arjun.\"\n\nThen, after contemplating on that, Arjuna began to prepare. One does not get, by deluding the mind, which is stronger than desire. 8 ”. Meaning of the word\n\nTam—on that; Param—only; Samanudhyayan— meditating; Antaram— appropriate opportunity; Prepsuha— awaited to be received;\nArjunah—Arjun; Nalebhe— could not experience; Sham— peace; Bhramat— distracted; Chittah— heart; Kamen— by desire;\nAti-balyasa— extremely powerful. Meditating on the same and waiting for the opportunity to take him away, Arjun was not getting peace.\nHe was not able to find peace. His heart was pounding with desire. Meaning: Even after being honored by Balarama, Arjuna could not appreciate their courteous hospitality, because he was extremely agitated. Arjun's being distracted and Balram changing disguises—Arjun not recognizing—these were both plans by God to enjoy his divine plays. The great pilgrimage, the chariot, the fort, the departed.\nJaharanumatah pitroah krishnas cha maharathah. 9. Lexicon"
