      "textEn": "3\n\nThey consider in the form and the jealous demons see them in the form of death.\"\n\nSatva, you, by your service, what else should I do for you? This is the suffering of the beings, which is beyond my sight. 9>. Meaning of the word\n\nSaha - He; Tvam - You; Shadhi - Give orders; Swa - Own; Bhrityaan - Servants; Naha - We; Kim - What; Deva - O Lord; Karavam - Should do; He - Oh; Etat - This; Antah - As the end of this; Nrnam - Of humans; Klesha - Trouble; Yat - That;\nBhavan - Yours; Akshi - Eyes; Go-charah - Visible. Oh Lord, You are the Supreme Being, and You are our Master Servant. How can we help you? Oh Lord, just by your sight, all the sufferings of human life come to an end. Srisuka said:\nHaving heard thus, the Lord, bowing down, said:\nHaving taken the water, he spoke thus. 50. Meaning of the word.\n\nShri-Shuka said—Shri Shukadeva Goswami said; Tat—by that (Shrutadeva); Uktam—was said; Iti—thus;\nUpakarnya—listening; Bhagavan—God; Pranata—of the surrendered; Aarti—of suffering; Ha—destroyer; Grihitva—capturing; Paniina—with one's hand; Paniim—his hand; Prahasan—laughing heartily; Tam—from him; Uvaacha—said..\n\nShri Shukdev Goswami said: Hearing these words from Shrutadev, the Lord, who removes the suffering of the surrendered,\ntook Shrutadev's hand in his own hand and, laughing, spoke to him in this way. Meaning: Acharya Vishwanath's commentary is that, as a sign of Lord Maitreya, holding Shrutadev's hand,\nhe laughed because he wanted to explain to him that, \"Okay, you know exactly about me,\nand I also know everything about you. Therefore, now I will tell you something special.\"\n\nShri Bhagavan said:\n\nFor the sake of the grace of Brahma, I have attained knowledge of the sages.\nThey are wandering in my world, again and again, with the dust of their feet. 51. Meaning of the word\n\nShri-Bhagavan said—Bhagavan said; Brahman—O Brahmin; Te—Yours; Anugraha—To give blessings; Arthaya—For the sake of;\nSampraaptaan—Having come; Viddh